==English==

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop|def=1|head=[[immaculate|Immaculate]] [[conception|Conception]]}}

# {{lb|en|Catholicism}} The [[doctrine]], in the [[Roman]] [[Catholic Church]], that the [[Virgin Mary]] was [[conceive]]d biologically but free from [[original sin]].
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholicism}} December 8th (The ''Feast of the Immaculate Conception of Mary'').
# {{lb|en|proscribed}} The conception or incarnation of [[Jesus]] as viewed by those who believe that he was conceived without sin.
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholicism}} {{n-g|A [[title]] of}} Mary, {{n-g|in particular reference to her unique status with regard to the aforementioned doctrine.}}

====Usage notes====
* Usage referring to the conception of Jesus (by Mary and the Holy Spirit) rather than that of Mary (by her human parents) is based on ignorance or misunderstanding of the original term and of the doctrine it refers to, but it is nonetheless relatively widespread.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|immaculism}}, {{l|en|immaculist}}
* {{l|en|maculism}}, {{l|en|maculist}}

